The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/new-apple-tv-4k-announced/">new Apple TV 4K</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/new-siri-remote-compatible-apple-tv-models/">updated Siri Remote</a> unveiled today have quite a few new features, as outlined in our all-in-one summary below.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/New-Apple-TV-4K-and-Siri-Remote-Have-These-14-New-Features-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070590" /><br/>
Here are 11 changes coming with the new Apple TV:<ul><br/>
  <li>A19 chip, for up to 50% faster CPU performance and up to twice as fast graphics performance compared to the previous model with the A15 chip.</li><br/>
  <li>8GB of RAM is very likely, up from 4GB of RAM in the previous model. However, this spec still needs to be confirmed.</li><br/>
  <li>Siri AI support, with an Apple Intelligence-enabled iPhone or iPad required for questions involving a user's personal context. Siri AI will also be available on the second-generation and third-generation Apple TV 4K models released in 2021 and 2022 on tvOS 27.2 and later, according to Apple.</li><br/>
  <li>Three built-in far-field microphones for hands-free Siri AI voice control, but you can continue to use the Siri Remote if you prefer.</li><br/>
  <li>Surround sound functionality with four HomePods — either four HomePod mini 2 speakers or matching front and rear pairs of HomePod mini 2 and full-sized HomePod 2 speakers. All previous models remain limited to two HomePods.</li><br/>
  <li>Wi-Fi 7 support, up from Wi-Fi 6 for the previous model.</li><br/>
  <li>Bluetooth 6 support, up from Bluetooth 5 for the previous model.</li><br/>
  <li>AV1 and VP9 video support.</li><br/>
  <li>There is now only a single 128GB configuration with an Ethernet port. The previous model also had a 64GB/Wi-Fi-only model.</li><br/>
  <li>The white status light has been centered on the front edge of the Apple TV 4K.</li><br/>
  <li>The new model is around 1% heavier than the previous model. (Hey, it counts).</li><br/>
</ul>Here are three changes coming with the new Siri Remote:<ul><br/>
  <li>Find My and Precision Finding support, making it easier to find the remote if it is misplaced. Precision Finding support for the Siri Remote requires an iPhone 17 or newer (excluding the iPhone 17e), iPhone Air, or iPhone Duo.</li><br/>
  <li>A built-in speaker that can play a sound to help you locate it.</li><br/>
  <li>The new remote is around 6% heavier than the previous version.</li><br/>
